---
import '../../styles/site.css';import{dbFrom,isConfigured,identityDbFrom}from'../../lib/db.js';const db=dbFrom(Astro.locals);const shared=Boolean(identityDbFrom(Astro.locals));const configured=db?await isConfigured(db):false;if(configured)return Astro.redirect('/admin/settings');
---
<main><h1>Set up your website</h1><p>This is the graphical handoff from deployment to site ownership. Normal setup does not require SQL, Wrangler, environment files, or source-code editing.</p>{!db?<section class="card"><h2>Deployment is not finished yet</h2><p>The application is running, but its database binding is not available. The eventual one-click deployment process will provision this automatically before sending the owner here.</p></section>:<form class="card" method="post" action="/api/setup/save"><h2>1. {shared ? 'Connect the owner and business' : 'Create the owner and business'}</h2>{!shared && <label>Your name<input name="name" autocomplete="name"></label>}<label>{shared ? 'Existing CallMeAllie owner/admin email' : 'Owner email'}<input name="email" type="email" required></label><label>{shared ? 'Existing CallMeAllie password' : 'Owner password'}<input name="password" type="password" minlength="10" required></label><label>Business name<input name="business_name" required></label><button>Save and continue</button></form>}<section class="card"><h2>What comes next in this wizard</h2><p>Branding → Stripe → email → products → licensing where applicable → system check → launch.</p></section></main>